                <pb facs="0841" n="713" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg713"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">714.1515/549a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-02-11T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. The Guatemalan Minister informs the Department that his Government is again
                    protesting to the Government of Honduras against violations of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">status quo</hi> in the disputed territory, and
                    particularly against the construction of a railway line between Cacao and
                    Chachagualillo.</p>
                <p>Please investigate and report, ascertaining especially whether any railway
                    construction is being carried on in the disputed territory.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
